  "prior_scope": "# Review \u2014 a9c4475d7cda parametric threshold prototype\nTask/source: `a9c4475d7cda` generator v3.0.0, SHA-256 `1e242e04c710107969f6da280291342ae2fe6f0dc4da2a7eb7652e17c85bbe51`, rule hash `8cfb5cf9c2c4`.\nDefect \u2192 repair: the approved generator was stable, but the assigned ARC family lacked a small parametric extension; added an isolated two-setting prototype instead of rewriting production.\nParameter: one fixed `min_panel_count \u2208 {2,3}` per episode; default `2` is byte-for-byte canonical and `3` changes only the pinned comparison literal.\nLesson evidence: two retained Racket-backed episodes, each with 3 demonstrations and 4 distinct queries; demonstrations alone identify the selected setting.\nFocused verification: 74/74 selected-task tests pass; the shared parametric worker also completed four 3-demo/4-query jobs with 40 protected-Racket evaluations and one unique demonstration survivor per requested setting.\nAdversarial verification: 32 seeds / 288 pairs plus 1-demo/8-query and 8-demo/1-query Racket boundaries passed with no remaining finding.\nReference-rule changes: none; `generator.py`, canonical examples, base solution authority, and approval state are unchanged.\nRemaining limits: only thresholds 2 and 3 are qualified; testing is finite; this remains a proposed task-local prototype, not production approval or training admission.\nDisposition: routine maintainer review of `workspace/parametric/promotion.json` and `adapter.py`; no urgent source repair is indicated.\nStorage-study note: `before_extract` was missed and was not reconstructed; `after_extract`, `after_setup`, and `before_package` are retained when available.\n",
